WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.433
AI in the CI pipeline.

2
00:00:02.733 --> 00:00:07.800
At a few thousand tests, flaky failures and slow runs quietly eat your team's trust.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Two problems dominate at scale: flaky tests, and slow, low signal runs.

4
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:23.133
ML based flaky detection scores each test's history against code changes, and quarantines tests that fail independently of what changed.

5
00:00:23.433 --> 00:00:29.367
Test impact analysis maps changed files to the tests that could be affected, and runs only those.

6
00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:35.600
And LLM triage clusters failures by their error text, so you read causes, not failures.

7
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.600
Look at the cost of running everything.

8
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:44.000
A forty minute end to end suite runs in full for a documentation only change.

9
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.000
With impact analysis, it drops to a ninety second smoke check.

10
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.233
Now, triage.

11
00:00:50.533 --> 00:00:52.200
Say eighty seven tests fail.

12
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.733
We embed each assertion and stack trace.

13
00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:56.967
Then we cluster them by similarity.

14
00:00:57.267 --> 00:01:00.767
A human sees three root causes, not eighty seven failures.

15
00:01:01.967 --> 00:01:05.367
In code, we embed the failure messages and cluster them.

16
00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:08.300
Eighty seven failures collapse into three groups.

17
00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:14.567
Sixty two are one checkout regression, nineteen are a flaky timeout, and six are a fixture bug.

18
00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:17.567
Here is how the numbers play out.

19
00:01:17.867 --> 00:01:21.800
A documentation PR no longer triggers the forty minute suite.

20
00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:28.300
A flaky detector flags a checkout test that fails thirty percent of the time, unrelated to any change.

21
00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:32.801
It is quarantined and ticketed, instead of blocking five PRs.

22
00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:34.867
And no test logic was touched.

23
00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:36.873
Let's recap.

24
00:01:36.873 --> 00:01:40.567
Flaky tests erode trust, so detect and quarantine them.

25
00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:43.600
Impact analysis runs only what matters.

26
00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.267
Triage clusters failures by root cause.

27
00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:49.967
And all of that works without touching a single test's logic.
